                <pb facs="0553" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1831/66 Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sack</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-18T13:00:00-04:00">September 18, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. With reference to your despatch No. 840, of September 6. You are authorized
                    to accept binding of the present rate on flour in view of your opinion that
                    insistence on a duty reduction will jeopardize conclusion of the trade
                    agreement. It is hoped that this substantial modification of our position will
                    clear the way for rapid and satisfactory conclusion of the agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
